## 4. Implementation Strategy

### 4.1 Phase-by-Phase Migration Plan

#### **Phase 1: Foundation (Week 1-2)**
**Objective:** Establish core data structures và database system

**Tasks:**
- [ ] Create ScriptableObject definitions
- [ ] Implement CharacterDatabase và GameDatabase
- [ ] Create basic CharacterDefinition entries cho existing characters
- [ ] Implement data loading và caching system
- [ ] Create migration tools cho existing prefabs

**Deliverables:**
- CharacterDatabase.asset với current characters
- GameDatabase.asset với team configurations
- Data migration scripts
- Basic caching system

**Risk Mitigation:**
- Keep existing system running in parallel
- Create data validation tools
- Implement rollback mechanisms

#### **Phase 2: Enhanced Character Controller (Week 3-4)**
**Objective:** Replace RagdollCharacter với EnhancedCharacterController

**Tasks:**
- [ ] Implement EnhancedCharacterController base class
- [ ] Create specialized manager components
- [ ] Implement character initialization system
- [ ] Add backward compatibility layer
- [ ] Create automated testing suite

**Migration Strategy:**
```csharp
// Backward compatibility approach
public class RagdollCharacterAdapter : MonoBehaviour
{
    private EnhancedCharacterController enhancedController;

    void Start()
    {
        // Migrate old RagdollCharacter to new system
        MigrateToEnhancedSystem();
    }

    void MigrateToEnhancedSystem()
    {
        RagdollCharacter oldController = GetComponent<RagdollCharacter>();
        if (oldController != null)
        {
            // Create enhanced controller
            enhancedController = gameObject.AddComponent<EnhancedCharacterController>();

            // Transfer data
            TransferCharacterData(oldController, enhancedController);

            // Disable old controller
            oldController.enabled = false;
        }
    }
}
```

#### **Phase 3: UI System Overhaul (Week 5-6)**
**Objective:** Implement new multi-step selection UI

**Tasks:**
- [ ] Design và implement UI panels
- [ ] Create 3D preview system
- [ ] Implement selection state management
- [ ] Add visual feedback systems
- [ ] Integrate với existing drag & drop

**UI Implementation Priority:**
1. **Category Selection Panel** - Basic grid layout
2. **Character Selection Panel** - Character cards với stats
3. **3D Preview System** - Real-time character preview
4. **Team Selection Panel** - Team color preview
5. **Final Preview Panel** - Complete configuration review

#### **Phase 4: Integration & Polish (Week 7-8)**
**Objective:** Full system integration và performance optimization

**Tasks:**
- [ ] Integrate new system với GameManager
- [ ] Implement object pooling
- [ ] Add save/load functionality
- [ ] Performance optimization
- [ ] Comprehensive testing

**Integration Checklist:**
- [ ] GameManager compatibility
- [ ] Battle system integration
- [ ] UI event handling
- [ ] Performance benchmarks
- [ ] Memory usage optimization

### 4.2 Backward Compatibility Approach

#### **Compatibility Layer Design:**
```csharp
public class LegacySystemBridge : MonoBehaviour
{
    public static bool useLegacySystem = false;

    public static void SpawnCharacter(Vector3 position, int teamID)
    {
        if (useLegacySystem)
        {
            // Use old BattleGameManager system
            BattleGameManager.Instance.SpawnCharacterAtPosition(position);
        }
        else
        {
            // Use new CharacterManagementSystem
            CharacterManagementSystem.Instance.SpawnCharacter(
                selectedCharacterID, selectedVariantID, teamID, position);
        }
    }
}
```

#### **Data Migration Tools:**
```csharp
[MenuItem("Tools/Character System/Migrate Legacy Data")]
public static void MigrateLegacyData()
{
    // Find all existing RagdollCharacter prefabs
    string[] prefabPaths = AssetDatabase.FindAssets("t:Prefab");

    foreach (string path in prefabPaths)
    {
        GameObject prefab = AssetDatabase.LoadAssetAtPath<GameObject>(
            AssetDatabase.GUIDToAssetPath(path));

        if (prefab.GetComponent<RagdollCharacter>() != null)
        {
            CreateCharacterDefinition(prefab);
        }
    }
}

static void CreateCharacterDefinition(GameObject prefab)
{
    RagdollCharacter ragdoll = prefab.GetComponent<RagdollCharacter>();

    CharacterDefinition definition = ScriptableObject.CreateInstance<CharacterDefinition>();
    definition.characterID = GenerateCharacterID(prefab.name);
    definition.displayName = prefab.name;
    definition.basePrefab = prefab;

    // Transfer stats
    definition.baseStats = new CharacterStats
    {
        maxHealth = ragdoll.maxHealth,
        moveSpeed = ragdoll.moveSpeed,
        attackDamage = ragdoll.attackDamage,
        attackRange = ragdoll.attackRange,
        attackCooldown = ragdoll.attackCooldown
    };

    // Save as asset
    string assetPath = $"Assets/Data/Characters/{definition.characterID}.asset";
    AssetDatabase.CreateAsset(definition, assetPath);
}
```

